# Art refresh — 2026-11-19

## Objective

Make the rounded A3 wisp load from the main development checkout and deliver the
remaining A2 artwork described in `docs/prompts/codex-art-prompts.md`.

## Context

The active checkout was `feat/M3c-host-stealth`, with the original one-cube nucleus
and ten ray bones in both art sources and runtime resources. The earlier rounded
revision lived only in `/tmp/wispborn-v1-rounding`; that directory no longer exists.
The committed V1 branch retained the first A3 version and its regeneration scripts.
The new `feat/V1-art-refresh` branch starts from the active checkout, preserving
F1, F2 and M3c. No temporary worktree is required for this delivery.

## Steps

1. Restore committed A3 sources and reconstruct the requested half-pixel chamfers.
2. Copy all four runtime assets into the main checkout; check generated resources
   and packaged JAR contents after the build.
3. Generate all A2 sprites, white bitmap glyphs, vignette, layout, variants and
   both mockups with original deterministic pixel art.
4. Validate dimensions/names against F4, alpha channels and source/export parity.
5. Record build and artifact validation separately from manual in-game review.

## Decisions

- Preserve the 5px nucleus diameter, rig, two halos and possession timing.
- Keep A2 artwork under `art/hud/`; F4 runtime HUD implementation is outside the
  user's request for the remaining artistic work.
- Use variant A for core and hunger in the mockups; retain visible alternatives.
- Keep generated sources and regeneration scripts in the durable repository.
- Technical A3 previews are not Blockbench or Minecraft captures.

## Open questions

- User visual review of rounded wisp in game, including transparency and distance.
- User selection/approval of A2 icons and layout before F4 runtime integration.
- V1 step 1 multiplayer checks and first-person code are not completed by an art update.

## Verification outcome

- A3 validator passed: rig, UVs, PNGs, animation parity and timing limits.
- A2 validator passed: all 24 sprite names/sizes, RGBA alpha, bitmap font and scaling.
- Both generators reproduced identical file hashes on a second run.
- Mockups inspected at 100% and 200%; vignette preview inspected separately.
- `./gradlew build`: BUILD SUCCESSFUL in 17s.
- All four wisp files match art, source resources, processed resources and packaged
  `build/libs/wispborn-0.0.1.jar`. Packaged nucleus has 27 cuboids and no ray bones.
- No manual in-game or Blockbench validation was performed in this session.
